WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(upbeat music playing)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:03.583
(crowd cheering)

00:00:04.908 --> 00:00:07.260
- So, I was talking to
Brian before we got here.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:08.093
Y'all know each other.

00:00:08.093 --> 00:00:09.240
You've known each other for, like, years.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.440
- For years and years.
- Many, many.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.810
And Robin, Brian's wife,
is one of my best friends,

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:14.910
and she was a bridesmaid at our wedding.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.290
And we were at their wedding.

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:17.123
- [Brian] Yeah.

00:00:17.123 --> 00:00:17.956
- [Kelly] And that's like,

00:00:17.956 --> 00:00:18.789
over 30 years.
- That's a long time ago.

00:00:18.789 --> 00:00:19.622
- A long time ago.

00:00:19.622 --> 00:00:21.390
- That's like for us, it's almost 35.

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:22.240
And for you-
- 34, then. Yeah.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.250
- Yeah. Exactly.
- Yeah.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.300
- Just one year apart.
- Yeah.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.133
Oh my gosh.

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:26.863
So wait, have y'all ever had, like,

00:00:26.863 --> 00:00:27.696
I mean in that time-

00:00:27.696 --> 00:00:29.730
- I haven't seen him since.
(laughs) (crowd laughing)

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.530
- [Kelly] I imagine
you've had a game night,

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.150
or a dinner, or some kind of fun thing

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:34.050
y'all have done together, right?

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.270
- Well, we've had many fun
things that we've done together.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:37.200
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- But there is

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.450
a really fun thing that we've done.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:42.180
And, sometimes, we have
a dinner at our party,

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.490
at our house called "Sing
for Your Supper Party."

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:46.980
And we tell people that they have to come,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.390
and they have to sing.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:49.710
And you don't have to be a singer.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:51.660
You can be anything in the business,

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.820
but you have to come,
you have to bring a song,

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.260
or you get no dinner.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.093
And-

00:00:56.093 --> 00:00:56.926
- What do you mean you
don't have to be a singer?

00:00:56.926 --> 00:00:58.592
So they don't have to sing?
- No. Like if-

00:00:58.592 --> 00:00:59.425
Let's say-
- Well, they have to sing.

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:00.510
- [Kelly] Oh.
- They have to sing.

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:03.120
But, you don't have to be
a professional to do it.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:03.953
As a matter of fact-
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:01:03.953 --> 00:01:05.670
- It's better if you're
not a professional.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:06.503
- Oh my God.

00:01:06.503 --> 00:01:07.590
This is like My Best Friend's Wedding,

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:09.270
when Cameron Diaz does
the karaoke. (laughs)

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.530
- It totally is like that. (laughs)

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:13.680
But you know, my pianist comes,
and he can play anything.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.720
And people just show up with their songs.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.630
And there have been many times that people

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:20.550
really impress you.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:21.383
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:01:21.383 --> 00:01:22.844
- In more ways than one.

00:01:22.844 --> 00:01:24.000
(crowd laughing)

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:24.833
Yes.

00:01:24.833 --> 00:01:27.150
- They dive deeper, or they really commit.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:28.140
- Exactly. Exactly.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:28.973
- [Kelly] Those are the people
I want at the dinner party.

00:01:28.973 --> 00:01:30.158
- Totally.
- The ones that really commit.

00:01:30.158 --> 00:01:31.173
- Yes.

